      "date": "2026-03-02",
      "authority": 90,
      "text": "Incident INC-031: 2 March 2026. Service degradation began 14:05 UTC and ended 15:20 UTC (75 minutes). Root cause: expired TLS certificate on the edge gateway. 12,400 customer transactions failed. The certificate expiry alert had been disabled on 1 March 2026 during maintenance."
    },
    {
      "id": "I2",
      "type": "incident_timeline",
      "title": "Incident INC-032 timeline",
      "date": "2026-03-04",
      "authority": 90,
      "text": "Incident INC-032: 4 March 2026. Service degradation began 09:10 UTC and ended 09:55 UTC (45 minutes). Root cause: a failed rollback of configuration change CHG-441. 3,100 customer transactions failed. The rollback failure was unrelated to the certificate incident."
    },
    {
      "id": "I3",
      "type": "root_cause_note",
      "title": "Root-cause note for INC-031",
      "date": "2026-03-03",
      "authority": 85,
      "text": "INC-031 root cause: the edge gateway certificate expired because the renewal job was not running and the expiry alert was disabled. Recommended remediation: rotate certificates automatically, re-enable expiry alerts, and add a weekly certificate inventory check."
    },
    {
      "id": "I4",
      "type": "draft_postmortem",
      "title": "Draft postmortem (not approved)",
      "date": "2026-03-05",
